# .trivyignore — accepted/deferred vulnerabilities (Phase V3-5, 2026-08-20)
#
# Context: Spring Boot was bumped 3.2.5 -> 3.2.12 (the FINAL OSS release of
# the 3.2.x line). The remaining 37 fixable CRITICAL/HIGH findings
# (5 CRITICAL, 32 HIGH — Trivy 0.74.0 DB) in the pom.xml analysis are fixed
# only in dependency lines bundled with Spring Boot 3.3+/3.4+
# (Spring Framework 6.2/7.0, Spring Security 6.3+, Jackson 2.18+,
# Tomcat 9.0.99+/10.1.40+, Netty 4.1.12x, Micrometer 1.15+).
# The 3.2.x line is EOL and will never receive those fixes.
#
# Decision: defer to a dedicated Spring Boot 3.4/3.5 upgrade sprint
# (documented in docs/history/optimalisasi-v3/06-final-report-phaseV3-5.md,
# backlog item). The CI Trivy gate remains ENABLED and will FAIL on any NEW
# CVE not listed below. Remove entries as the upgrade lands.
